course: dictionary
lesson: 10123
title: Many meanings of thought
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word thought can work in different ways. Sometimes it is a verb, the past of think: «I thought it was Monday.» Here thought tells us what the speaker believed a while ago, so it is about thinking.
explain: Sometimes thought is a noun, an idea that comes into your mind. «The smell of hot cabbage gives Toad new and inspiring thoughts.» Toad's thoughts are his ideas, the new ideas that pop into his head.
explain: Thought can also mean careful thinking. «Give it some thought» means think about it carefully before you decide. Look at the words around thought to work out which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Thought is the past of think. The forms are think, thinks, thought and thinking.
fact: A thought is an idea or opinion that comes into your mind.
fact: «I thought so» means I had already believed that.
fact: «It's the thought that counts» means the kindness behind a present matters more than what it costs.
fact: «Deep in thought» and «lost in thought» both mean thinking so hard that you do not notice what is around you.
exercise: In «I thought it was Monday», thought is a form of which word? | thin | *think | thank | thing
exercise: «The smell of hot cabbage gives Toad new and inspiring thoughts.» What are the thoughts here? | Hot food on a plate | Walks in the countryside | *Ideas that come into his mind | Loud noises from the kitchen
exercise: Grandma gives Ella a cheap card and says, «It's the thought that counts.» What does she mean? | The card must cost a lot to be good | Thoughts cannot be counted | *The kindness behind the card matters most | She wants the card back
test: «She was lost in thought and did not hear the bell.» What does lost in thought mean? | Very angry with the bell | *Thinking so hard she did not notice things around her | Playing a word game | Lost on the way to school
test: Which word is the past of think? | thank | thinking | *thought | thinks
exam: In «Give it some thought», what does thought mean? | Throw it in the bin | Give it away to a friend | *Careful thinking about it | Ignore it completely
